Pinned snapshots
----------------
leope/ark-asr-0.6B-mlx  6ec069bd68cbbe165aa42728eac482c90cb58d2f
leope/ark-asr-3B-mlx    63d9fb8ba352c5c7c65ff2336019048170563d63

The nine vendored modules are byte-identical between the two snapshots, so a
single copy serves both the 0.6B and the 3B backend.

Vendored verbatim
-----------------
__init__.py, api.py, cache.py, config.py, decoder.py, encoder.py,
generation.py, model.py, processor.py

No edits were made: the files are byte-for-byte copies of the upstream
snapshot. Modifications, if any are ever needed, must be recorded here.

Omitted
-------
cli.py         — command-line entry point, unused by the sidecar.
conversion.py  — PyTorch -> MLX weight converter; requires torch, which
                 Voiceour does not ship. The weights we download are already
                 converted.

Why vendored
------------
The upstream model repositories ship their runtime as Python source inside the
model repo. Fetching and importing that source at runtime would mean the app
executes code downloaded from Hugging Face. Vendoring the runtime here keeps
every line of executed code in this repository and under review, and lets the
model cache fetch weights and tokenizer assets only (see cache.ARK_06B /
cache.ARK_3B allow_patterns).
